From: ioswitch <noreply@ioswitch.local>
Subject: [PATCH] A read-only shader cache seed beneath the directory

Every process opening the device kept its own shader cache directory, and only backboardd got a seed: the plugin copied
a host-made cache (1,017 files) into backboardd's directory at its first device open of a build, ~7 s synchronously,
and every other process compiled from nothing. METAL2VULKAN_SHADER_CACHE_SEED now names a directory laid out as a
cache directory, read beneath the device's own: an entry or record the directory does not have is read under the same
name from the seed, and a miss in both compiles and writes the directory's own entry as before (found first from then
on). The seed is never written, scanned, trimmed, removed from or touched (no access time): it may sit on a read-only
volume and be shared by every process. A seed hit costs the directory's failed open and the seed file's read, where a
directory hit costs the read and an access-time write. ShaderCacheStatistics::seed_reads counts the seed's accepted
reads. Entry and record names hash the build, the key and the device's profile fingerprint, none of them per process,
so one seed serves every process of the build that made it.
